    "plain": "Expanding the British Business Bank aims to give more small businesses access to funding, which could create jobs and raise wages \u2014 but the projected gains are uncertain and will take years to materialise, if they do at all.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the BBB's expanded lending and investment actually creates net new, good-quality jobs at scale, or merely substitutes for private finance that would have flowed anyway (deadweight).",
